Z||000000||fieroburton||07-19-2001||11:54 PM||||does any body know any thing about these engines ? I plan on putting one in my 84<BR>so I can beat that supra . I found a place that has them called the fiero shop , in canada. does any body own one of these ?<BR>if so who can put the engine in or can you do it your self with out engine smarts ?<P>------------------<BR>1984 2M4 SE <BR>    <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fieroburton/1.html" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/fieroburton/1.html</A> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Joe Torma||07-20-2001||12:09 AM||||I stroked my 2.8 to a 3.1 and it ran awesomely for 5 years...I just moved up to the 3400.<P>225hp?  I would say 200.  And I had a real hot cam.<P>Joe<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/3400.gif">   ||||reg||1
Z||000002||fieroburton||07-20-2001||12:21 AM||||do you buy a hole new engine or take it to a shop and have it done there?<BR>were can i get some one to do that ?<P>how was you burn outs ?<P>------------------<BR>1984 2M4 SE <BR>    <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fieroburton/1.html" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/fieroburton/1.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Uaana||07-20-2001||01:27 AM||||Burton, Nice looking 84, <BR>There are a few ways to get this done.<BR>1. buy a 3.1 from a Lumina<BR>2. buy a 2.8 and have someone install a stroker kit.<BR>3. Just buy a 3.4 and forget the 3.1<BR>After you get the engine you will have to find someone to install it. I'd ask around the OH Fiero club.<BR>It will probably cost you a bit more than what you may have heard because of the 4 to 6 swap is not as easy as 6 to 6.<BR>As for getting the engines it's pretty easy call around your local salvage/recycle yards.<BR>I got my 3.4 for $450 the install will be quite a bit more. (my mechanic asked me not to tell how much he's charging)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>A good starting point would be to go search the tech section. Just put in 3.1 or 3.4 swap and you will find pages of information that cover this.<P>Good luck and don't get frustrated when things go wrong (they will you own a 17yo car)||||reg||6
Z||000004||Formula||07-20-2001||08:54 AM||||the 3.2 in my fiero supposedly put out 270 horspower on the dyno for the previous owner in a blazer.  I'm skeptical of this but I was told that the blazer could so a wheel stand and do massive burnouts.  Since he ran a really good set of headers and I'm running Fiero exhaust my guess would be that I should 200 + horspower, esp. if he's telling the truth about the dyno numbers.  btw.. he put over $3000 in building the engine then I've put at least another thousand into it making it fit the fiero.  When its in I'll take it to the track and see if its more then a usual 3.2 and if it is I'll find the specs for it.<P>I know it was at least balanced, blue printed, C&Ced, Huge Cam, bored out, shaved heads, everything was ported and polished.  now it has a high volume fiero oil pump, a fiero windage tray, less pulleys on it, no AC or power steering, edlebrock thruster 2 ported intake. Holley 4 bbl 390 carb. (I bought this saying it was a 3.2 @ 7000 rpms). I guess it has A LOT of stuff done to the heads.<P>but like I said, I want track proof before I believe it has that much power.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigformulagt.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||fieroburton||07-20-2001||09:27 AM||||thanks a whol lot<BR>il start looking today<P>------------------<BR>1984 2M4 SE <BR>    <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fieroburton/1.html" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/fieroburton/1.html</A> ||||reg||7
Z||000006||Joe Torma||07-20-2001||10:32 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fieroburton:<BR><B>do you buy a hole new engine or take it to a shop and have it done there?<BR>were can i get some one to do that ?<P>how was you burn outs ?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It was my first attempt at rebuilding an engine!  I bought the kit from PISA.  I don't think they sell it anymore.  Dumped the COMPUCAM I had in it after 6 months.  I started working for Fieo Specialties and Rich gave me one of his cams...Nice Burnouts.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Actually the car always just hooked up and took off!  My brother has a worked up 305 Camaro and my 3.1 SE was neck and neck with him in a race...and he jumped the light!<P>I've driven my 3400 only twice so far...I half-got-on-it and it is amazing.<P>I'd do the 3.4 conversion...the 3400 is a pain.  Make sure you have someone port out the intake and heads.  Get some decent hedders.  The 3.4 is a whole lot more torquey.  Burnouts good.<P>Joe||||reg||1
